_to_delete/
# Session scratch, same category as _to_delete/ above. `_xfer` is transit archives moving files
# between a cloud session and this machine; `_scratch` is built pages and one-off recordings
# kept for a second look. Everything in either is regenerable from a command in the tree -- a
# recording is `record_sow_offers.py --scenario X`, a page is its generator -- so committing
# them would only mean two copies, one of which nothing updates.
_xfer/
_scratch/
pilgrim_optimizer.egg-info/
*.tar.gz

# Scratch from generator sessions: experiments, probe renders, one-off scripts. Ignored rather than
# merely untracked, for two reasons. It is 198 MB, which makes it the one thing here that a
# `git add -A` must never reach. And its half-finished scripts were the only hits `ruff check
# --select F` reported in this working tree, while CI -- which sees tracked files -- was clean: a
# check that fails on scratch is a check you learn to skim past.
Claude outputs/

# Concept art: the folder is committed, these two parts of it are not.
#
# _reference/ holds third-party images kept for inspiration and never used in the game. Looking at
# one is fine; committing it would put somebody else's work in every clone forever, and the credit
# we would have to write beside it would probably name the wrong person -- a Pinterest link is a
# re-post, not an artist. The manifest records the URL so the reference survives without the file,
# and build_browser.py draws a card that links out when the file is not there.
ui/concept/_reference/
